          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "<strong>How to Introduce Your Cat to the Scratch Box</strong>",
            "heading_size": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text_cE7LyU": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<ol><li><strong>Prime with familiar scents</strong> – rub a towel on your cat’s face or inside the box.<br/><br/></li><li><strong>Use interactive rewards</strong> – place treats or sprinkle catnip near scratch surfaces.<br/><br/></li><li><strong>Replicate natural placement</strong> – situate near their favorite stretching areas, like next to a window or post-nap spot.<br/><br/></li></ol><p><strong>Encourage with play</strong> – feather toys traced along the box edges attract cats quickly.<br/><br/></p>"
          }
        }
      },
